A 5 GHz access point started through this driver never beacons. It reports
success -- start_ap waits for the firmware answer and the answer arrives -- but
nothing goes out on the air, so the SSID never appears in a scan.

The channel is only ever in the beacon. WIFI_CMD_START_AP carries a length and
the beacon bytes and nothing else, and hostapd does not put a DS Parameter Set
in a 5 GHz beacon at all (src/ap/beacon.c writes one for B and G modes only).
The one thing the firmware is told about 149 is the HT Operation element in the
tail, and that is evidently not where it looks.

So when the head carries no DS Parameter Set and the tail has an HT Operation,
append one with that element primary channel. The head is allocated with 32
bytes to spare, so three more fit.

The same fix as openwrt-uwe5622-sunxi 0539b491 ("Fix 5GHz AP"), which closed
the known issue "5 GHz AP mode not working" on this chip.

--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -1004,6 +1004,28 @@
 		memcpy(tail, beacon->tail, beacon->tail_len);
 		head_len = beacon->head_len;
 		tail_len = beacon->tail_len;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A 5 GHz beacon carries no DS Parameter Set: hostapd writes one only
+	 * for B and G modes. The firmware takes the AP channel from the IEs in
+	 * this beacon and from nowhere else, so without this the beacon goes
+	 * out on whatever channel the radio was last on, or not at all.
+	 */
+	if (!cfg80211_find_ie(WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS,
+			      ((struct ieee80211_mgmt *)head)->u.beacon.variable,
+			      head_len)) {
+		const u8 *ie = cfg80211_find_ie(WLAN_EID_HT_OPERATION,
+						tail, tail_len);
+
+		if (ie) {
+			wl_ndev_log(L_ERR, ndev,
+				    "no DS params, channel %d from HT operation\n",
+				    *(ie + 2));
+			head[head_len++] = WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS;
+			head[head_len++] = 1;
+			head[head_len++] = *(ie + 2);
+		}
 	}
 
 	sprdwl_change_beacon(vif, beacon);
